& [Fold1Identity] separates registry record and handle
  + registry is one volatile content-addressed process snapshot
  + record owns one exact context and either current checkpoint or terminal outcome
  + handle is a compact projection naming registry session sequence record and current state digests

& [Fold2Lifecycle] is OPEN ADVANCE INSPECT READ
  + OPEN parses one bounded exact context JSON and creates genesis
  + ADVANCE compare-and-sets registry session sequence and record then runs one bounded core step slice
  + INSPECT returns the compact handle while READ returns exact record JSON
  + process exit discards all state

& [Fold3Integrity] validates every boundary
  + registry record and handle digests cover all fields except their own digest
  + map keys sequence state checkpoint outcome and digest shapes are checked before every command
  + stale duplicate changed corrupt terminal or unknown-session commands do not mutate state

& [Fold4Concurrency] admits one equal-head writer
  + MCP serializes pure transitions under one process-local mutex
  + two callers using the same predecessor can produce at most one successor
  + every successful mutation increments registry generation and session sequence

& [Fold5CompactSchema] avoids recursive model-facing forms
  + MCP OPEN carries context_json string while READ returns record_json string
  + ADVANCE and INSPECT expose only identities digests sequence and quota
  + internal parsing remains strict typed and core-validated

& [Fold6Proof] measures both semantics and size
  + direct open advance inspect read and terminal flows match stateless core
  + stale concurrent and corrupt registry cases fail closed
  + official client proves one real subprocess and tool
  + metadata and ordinary ADVANCE payload sizes are recorded against the stateless baseline

& [Fold7Boundary] keeps custody local and temporary
  + no disk database restart recovery authentication network provider model prompt effect or production authority exists
  + digest identity is not producer authentication
  + compact JSON strings reduce schema expansion but do not change semantic types

& [SelectedFlow] is exact context JSON -> typed OPEN -> digest handle -> CAS ADVANCE -> inspectable READ -> terminal record or process exit

